# humanoid.pwe — a detailed simulated humanoid (a person-like figure) walking,
# expressed in PWE and rendered by the viewer. Limbs, fingers, torso and legs
# are **tapered capsules** (`shape = capsule; size = (radius_bottom, length,
# radius_top)` — a smooth, optionally tapered surface of revolution), the head
# and joints are spheres, facial detail (eyes, brows, nose, mouth) and shoes are
# boxes. Every part's world position and Z-angle is placed by the gait
# kinematics in its `update` rule; the viewer draws them via the entity
# `shape`/`size`/`color`/`label` attributes. Parts set `label = false`; the
# viewer's 🏷 button toggles labels.
